Andy: Yeah, that's part of my philosophy for doing&nbsp;
it in the first place. I'm not selling a book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:15.760
I'm not selling a seat in a seminar, I just want&nbsp;
to see better movies. I'm a bit of an old grouch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.760
I guess but I don't think I'm alone in saying that&nbsp;
there aren't a lot of great movies anymore. We're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:26.600
lucky to see one a year, literally one good movie&nbsp;
a year much less the barrage of great films that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:32.760
grew up watching in the in the 70s, especially&nbsp;
when I came of age as a film watcher and fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:38.480
in love with films every week there'd be two or&nbsp;
three great films released and now it's there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:47.840
a paucity, there's just a lack of of good movies&nbsp;
because I believe the craft of screenwriting has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:54.000
fallen to such a low level there's a lot of&nbsp;
reasons for it doesn't really matter why but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:07:00.920
my goal here is just to share what I know and I&nbsp;
have learned a lot over 45 years of getting paid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:07.360
to do this I have learned a lot about how to&nbsp;
tell stories in the filmic medium so that's my&nbsp;&nbsp;

